            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> macos-13 was the last non-arm64 runner that was freely available, so when doing this, we can remove all the handling of x86_64 macos in CI.\r\n\r\nRight, actually https://github.com/actions/runner-images/issues/13046 points out that.\r\n> Workflows that depend on x86_64 (Intel CPU) can be migrated to use the macos-15-intel label, which is currently planned as the last supported image based on Intel CPU.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> (Also, what you wrote will always evaluate to 'macos-15' since it's truthy, you probably want a matrix w/ something like `runners: [macos-15, macos-14]` if you want this to run on both those arm64 runners.)\r\n\r\nAh, now everything makes more sense.",
            "commit_id": "9a0ed93d0e97581e82f9aeb61432a051c54492dc",
            "created_at": "2025-12-12T10:07:43Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@ jobs:\n         arch: [arm64, x86_64]\n         exclude:\n           - arch: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' && !contains(github.event.pull_request.labels.*.name, 'packaging') && 'arm64' }}\n-    runs-on: ${{ matrix.arch == 'arm64' && 'macos-14' || 'macos-13' }}\n+    runs-on: ${{ 'macos-15' || 'macos-14' }}",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/TokTok/qTox/pull/616#discussion_r2613655663",
